# Belt-and-braces secret protection for agent/.
#
# The root .gitignore already covers every pattern below. This file exists
# anyway, deliberately duplicating them, because the thing it guards against
# is not a missing rule - it is the root file being edited, truncated, or
# rewritten by a tool, and nobody noticing until a key is already in a commit.
#
# The asymmetry is the whole argument: a redundant ignore rule costs nothing
# and is never noticed, while a leaked API key cannot be un-leaked. `git rm
# --cached` removes it from the tip, not from history - the key still has to
# be revoked and rotated. Cheap insurance against an expensive, irreversible
# mistake.
#
# Two independent files must both fail for a secret to escape. Keep it that
# way: if a new secret-bearing file is added here, add it to the root too.

# ---------- Secrets ----------
# The real key lives in agent/.env. .env.example - the template, fake values
# only - IS committed, hence the negation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------- Virtual environment ----------
# agent/ has its own venv, separate from backend/.venv. Rebuilt from
# requirements.txt, never committed.
.venv/
venv/

# ---------- Python bytecode and caches ----------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
